# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/

# expo-env.d.ts is deliberately tracked, unlike in the stock template. Without it
# `tsc --noEmit` fails on the CSS side-effect import in src/constants/theme.ts, and it is
# only generated by running `expo start`/`expo prebuild`. Committing the three lines keeps
#
# `expo start` re-adds it to the generated expo-cli block at the bottom of this file every
# time it runs. That entry is inert: git does not apply .gitignore to a file that is already
# tracked. Do not bother deleting it — it comes straight back.
# `npm ci && npm run check` working on a fresh clone and in CI.

